    "description": {
     "value": "<p>He cannot say whether anyone ever played him. What he remembers is being drawn: four panels at a time, one summer, in a camp newspaper, until the strip stopped mid-story. He speaks in short lines, as if he has to fit inside a speech balloon, and every so often he finishes a thought with 'To be continued!' and waits, a little hopefully, for next week.</p>",
